5. Maintaining Legal Compliance Without Expensive Software
Missouri law requires parents to maintain basic record-keeping documentation showing subjects taught and daily instructional hours accrued . This documentation serves as your primary legal protection under state statute .
Fortunately, achieving legal compliance does not require purchasing expensive subscription software . A simple physical ledger or a free digital spreadsheet tracking the date, subject category (Core vs. Non-Core), location (Home vs. Away), and time spent satisfies all legal record-keeping standards outlined under RSMo § 167.012 .
